    <!-- ==========================================================================
         THE DEPOSITS - four reasons to leave the base

         WHAT WAS MISSING
         Every material in this mod came from a vanilla ore, a loot container, the
         trader or the farm. Nothing anywhere gave the player a reason to go to a
         PLACE. recipes.xml has claimed since v0.1 that the intermediates are
         "cheap to make and annoying to source"; for flux that was simply not true,
         because sand and bone are everywhere.

         THE LADDER
         Each deposit feeds one bottleneck, and its biome sets its price in risk.
         It is the same ladder the archetypes use, deliberately - by Cycle 3 a
         player already knows what the wasteland costs, so a wasteland-only
         material is a decision rather than a surprise.

           Limestone   everywhere, forest included   flux          tier 1
           Bitumen     desert, burnt forest          polymer       tier 2
           Sulphur     burnt forest, wasteland       reagent base  tier 2
           Scheelite   wasteland only                carbide       tier 3

         Limestone being in the starter biomes is not a break of the "starter
         biomes stay clean" rule from entitygroups.xml. That rule is about what
         can kill you. Flux is a day-ten need and must not require a trip to
         somewhere that will.

         NOTHING REQUIRES THESE
         Every recipe they feed keeps its original route, and the deposit route is
         added alongside. World placement is the one genuinely unverifiable part of
         this mod (VERIFY-25), so it is arranged such that a placement patch that
         matches nothing costs an efficiency and an errand - never a supply line,
         and never a deadlock.

         VERIFY-26: the Extends base below is a vanilla ore block, and it is a NEW
         vanilla dependency - everything else in this mod extends names it already
         depended on. If "terrOreIron" is wrong, all four deposits are wrong the
         same way, which is why they all use one base. Fallbacks to try in order:
         terrOreCoal, terrOreLead, oreIron.
         ========================================================================== -->

